R&C patch 7116: keep the word an idle RSX fetches when the guest moves put (gcm walker). Upstream candidate (general
runtime + lifter fix; not yet proposed upstream). Built from the preplan draft-h1-walker-race.patch with all the
review fixes (work/coord/preplan-1123/ffa/review.md). NOT run in a game yet: host tests only.

Problem (H1, walker race). Facts:
- [read in code] Full Frontal Assault 0x006F6138 (lifted ppu_recomp_035.cpp, func_006F6138), frame end, first
  injector: writes JUMP B at GET, the JUMP-back 0x20000000 | GET at the block's end (EA 0x406080B8), sync, put = that
  slot (0x006080B8, l.11674-11676); waits get == put (0x0079C2F0, lr 0x6F6438); then put = GET and the old word back
  at GET (l.11241-11244), with no wait for the RSX to take the JUMP-back; then resets the per-frame scratch ring the
  block came from. The same "put back to GET, no wait" shape is read in Into the Nexus 1.01 0x005F8AF8 (first
  injector) and the second injectors FFA 0x0073A4EC, Nexus 1.01 0x0063D3F4, A4O 0x006DC25C, ACiT 1.20 0x005F46F0
  (work/coord/decomp-q-1123/ffa-inject.md + -check.md). Whether the non-FFA sites run is not measured.
- [read in code] The walker reads put once per pass on the frame thread (cellGcmSys.c gcm_rsx_process_fifo_unlocked),
  and nothing wakes it on a PPU put store.
- [measured] ls-ffa-newgame-luamsg-1120-124120: put = 0x006080B8, the walker resumes there, decodes 0x49FC9A00
  (scratch data), CALL 0x14 / FEED0001, "FIFO JUMP to unmapped", resync to put; ~1 flip per 6 s in phoenix_ph1.
- [read, src:rpcs3-rsxfifo, behaviour only, nothing copied] RPCS3's puller re-reads put on every idle poll, fetches
  the word at get right after put moves and executes from its fetch cache; its FFA reference run shows no FIFO error.
- [read in code] Lifted stores do NOT reach the out-of-line vm_write32 in a default run: the generated ppu_recomp.h
  stores inline (vm_write32_mm) whenever vm_mm_st_ok passes, and the control register (inject base 0x7F000000 +
  0x2000 in the R&C port) is inside the inline span. Only PPU_WVAL / PPU_WWATCH / PT (vm_inline_st_ok = 0), the
  barrier watch, a null sweep, or an SPU reservation on the line sent it out of line. The preplan draft's hook was
  therefore dead in every run without a write watch (review.md s.1).

Fix:
- tools/ppu_lifter.py (the ppu_recomp.h template): ppu_mm gets `put` (= ppu_hle_inject_base + 0x2000, beside the
  load side's `poll`). vm_write32_mm stores inline only when ea != put; vm_write64_mm only when [ea, ea + 8) does not
  overlap [put, put + 4). So the guest's stw to put goes out of line in every run, as the 32-bit load of the ref-poll
  word already does; every other store keeps the inline path. Both define forms use it: vm_write32_inl (outside a
  lifted function) and the per-function `vm_write32(a, v) vm_write32_mm(&_mm, a, v)` (PPU_MM_SNAP). Cost: one more
  compare per inline 32/64-bit store (not measured). 8/16-bit and raw (vector, byte-reversed, dcbz) stores are not
  turned away: ASSUMPTION, no title moves put with them (every put store read is stw).
  EVERY TITLE NEEDS A RE-LIFT (the header is generated) and a rebuild.
- runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp: vm_write32 calls g_gcm_put_hook(v) when the EA is g_gcm_put_ea, after the OOB / null
  checks and BEFORE the store lands; vm_write64 does the same for a std whose high (ea == put) or low (ea == put - 4)
  word is put. An unaligned overlap is not hooked (ASSUMPTION, as above).
- libs/video/cellGcmSys.c:
  - g_gcm_put_ea / g_gcm_put_hook are defined here (beside ppu_hle_inject_base), so a binary that links libgcm
    without the PPU loader links as before; static forward declarations before cellGcmInit, which arms the hook.
  - gcm_note_ppu_put (guest thread): if new put != old put AND the published get == old put (the walker is parked
    there, so the next word it fetches is that one), it keeps ONE word, {old put, word at old put}, in one slot
    (seq_cst exchange, before the guest's store lands). The walker's next fetch at that offset takes the kept word,
    once. It keeps one word, not the span [old put, new put): later words of the span are read from memory as before.
    That covers FFA's single JUMP-back word; a title that reuses later words of the span before the walker's next pass
    is not covered.
  - The slot is dropped on a resync (gcm_fifo_resync_why), when a pass starts at another offset, by a newer keep
    (counted as dropped), and by the runtime's own put stores, which do not go through the hook: the two ring
    recycle paths and cellGcm_syscall_set_fifo.
  - Counter line `[gcm-putsnap] <when>: hook=N kept=N used=N changed=N dropped=N (mode M)`: every
    GCM_PUT_SNAP_STATS seconds of walker passes (default 30, 0 = exit only) and at exit (atexit). hook = guest put
    stores seen, kept = words kept, used = kept words taken by the fetch, changed = of those, words memory no longer
    held, dropped = kept words never used. `[gcm-putsnap] io=... now X, was Y when put moved off it` for the first 16
    changed words and then every power of two. `[gcm-putsnap] armed: ...` once at cellGcmInit.
  - Knobs: GCM_PUT_SNAP=0/off/false/no (hook not armed), =log (keep and compare, walk memory: the old behaviour, the
    discriminator), default on. GCM_PUT_SNAP_LOG=<n> logs the first n kept words. Do not combine with
    GCM_GET_EQ_PUT=1 (it publishes get = put, so the parked test always passes).
Why this matches the console [read in code + src:rpcs3-rsxfifo; behaviour in a game: guess until run]: an idle RSX
fetches that word within microseconds of the put move, and by then it is final (titles write commands before moving
put). A walker that is behind is unchanged (nothing is kept), like a busy RSX. Not a timeout, skip or clamp: it
restores the fetch order. Not the "cache the word when parking" idea game-side.md s.6 rejects (that copy would be taken
before the title appends); this one is taken at the put store. "Both FFA put stores are covered whatever the pass
timing" is a guess: it holds only if the overwrite of the slot lands after the restore store, and a writer off the
0x006F6138 path (another thread, an SPU, the third injector) is not excluded.

Tests (host, no game data):
- port/rc/tests/run_gcm_put_snap_test.sh: test_gcm_put_snap.c (the real walker, FFA's frame-end inject played in
  GCM_PUT_SNAP on / log / off; behind-walker case; set_fifo, resync and stale-pass drops; both ring recycle paths
  dropping a pending keep; a std with put as its low word; the counters). The guest's put stores run the tree's own
  vm_write32 / vm_write64 hook lines, extracted verbatim by port/rc/tests/put_hook_lines.py (which also checks they sit
  after the OOB guard and before the store). test_put_store_route.py: the lifter template routes the put store out of
  line and nothing else. Negative controls: the route test against the tree without this patch fails 24 of 307
  checks; the extractor fails on a ppu_loader.cpp without it; removing either recycle path's gcm_put_snap_forget(),
  vm_write64's low-word branch or its put-EA-0 guard, or moving vm_write32's hook after the store fails the test.
Runs needed before merge (coordinator): re-lift + rebuild every title that is built (tools/lift.sh: tods, acit120,
nexus101, ffa, a4o, qfb, dlhd, collection, collection_rc1, collection_rc2, collection_rc3; acit / nexus are the
disc-1.00 lifts, not built), then FFA newgame (the fix) and the guards in work/coord/preplan-1123/ffa/plan.md s.5
(G1-G5), each recording the counter line; FFA must show hook > 0, kept > 0.

